{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Runs ONE bounded step of an ACCEPTED kb.plan item (the GATED plan-item autonomy seam). The human move_item to `accepted` is the authorization. Gate: only entries tagged accepted are eligible - proposed/in-progress/done/abandoned are refused (the agent never self-promotes). CONVERGENCE GUARD: the count of prior steps is the entry's step_log length; at/over MAX_PLAN_STEPS (agent runtime setting, default 20, cap 1000 - deliberately SEPARATE from TOOL_BUDGET, which is a per-turn chatTurn round limit) it refuses with action needs_reapproval and a human must re-accept (move_item) to re-arm. Eligibility requires a STRUCTURED `step` field {lib,ctl,cmd,args?}; pure-prose intent is a no-op (action surfaced), never an LLM guess. Before acting it re-checks the entry's source-pointer hash and defers to the stale path on drift. The step executes panic-contained via Command::lookup, the result is appended to the entry's step_log, and the whole facet is written back through journaled patch_control_facet under the base hash - on stale_base it aborts and reports current_hash, never forces. One step per call; the executive's drive budget is the throttle. base is the board hash from agent.plan.board. Returns steps_taken/max_steps.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;","params":[{"name":"claim","type":"String"},{"name":"base","type":"String"},{"name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"opjijl1a158e0142bq1bd6","readers":[],"time":1792513165581,"username":"system","writers":[]}